Subject: [PATCH 23/38] Keep navigation pages, push values and draw toolbars on
 Linux

NavigationStack keeps every page in the graph and shows the top one, so a
page keeps its state under the pages pushed over it. It takes a path
binding (NavigationPath or a collection), pushes values through
navigationDestination(for:), isPresented and item destinations, and
NavigationLink(value:). Each page has an iOS bar: the large or inline
title, a back button titled with the page below, and toolbar items from
ToolbarItem, ToolbarItemGroup, navigationBarItems or a plain toolbar,
plus a bottom bar. dismiss pops a pushed page. Links in list rows show a
chevron, and a Form's background shows behind the bar.
