+// Iris: a navigation stack drawn by SwiftUI with iOS's look, until upstream has navigation.
+// Every page stays in the view graph with the top one shown, so a page keeps its state under
+// the pages pushed over it (and is not told it disappeared). A page's bar shows its title,
+// large unless inline, a back button titled with the page below, and its toolbar items.
+// ponytail: no push transition or swipe back, and a view pushed by a NavigationLink keeps the
+// destination the link had when tapped.
+
+/// systemBlue.
+private let systemBlue = Color(red: 0, green: 122 / 255, blue: 1)
